$ todoer pr submit --branch main -n 'First try' [cwd: fix-sum]
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: "First try" is not a pull request name - use first-try

$ todoer pr submit --branch main -n first-try [cwd: fix-sum]
submitted first-try: 1 commit, 3 files, into main
.todoer/prs/first-try on main, in the checkout <tmp>/repo
committed on main

$ todoer pr close first-try
closed first-try

$ git log --format=%s -1 && ls .todoer
todoer: close first-try
prs
todos

$ todoer pr submit --branch main -n second-try --todo fix-the-sum [cwd: fix-sum]
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: fix-sum has changes that are not committed: notes.txt - commit them first

$ todoer pr submit --branch main -n second-try --todo fix-the-sum [cwd: fix-sum]
submitted second-try: 1 commit, 3 files, into main
.todoer/prs/second-try on main, in the checkout <tmp>/repo
todos: fix-the-sum
committed on main

$ todoer pr submit --branch main -n third-try [cwd: fix-sum]
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: the pull request of fix-sum is second-try - a submit cannot rename it to third-try

$ todoer pr submit --branch main -n second-try [cwd: fix-sum]
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: the pull request second-try exists - pick another name, or use --update to replace its patch

$ todoer pr submit --branch main -n second-try --update -m 'From a new branch.' [cwd: fix-sum]
updated second-try: 1 commit, 3 files, into main
.todoer/prs/second-try on main, in the checkout <tmp>/repo
todos: fix-the-sum
committed on main

$ todoer pr ls && git log --format=%s -1 && git status --short
second-try  no comments  fix-sum-2 -> main  me@example.com
todoer: update second-try

$ todoer pr merge second-try
merged second-try into main
done: fix-the-sum
--- stderr
warning: not committed - the checkout has other changes: notes.txt. The changes of todoer are in the working tree. Commit them yourself

$ git log --format=%s -1 && git status --short
todoer: update second-try
 D .todoer/prs/second-try/pr.diff
 D .todoer/prs/second-try/pr.md
 D .todoer/prs/second-try/pr.patch
 D .todoer/todos/fix-the-sum.md
M  docs/guide.md
 M notes.txt
M  src/app.rs
R  src/old.rs -> src/lib.rs

$ todoer pr merge second-try --no-commit
merged second-try into main
done: fix-the-sum
not committed (--no-commit) - the changes are in the working tree

$ git log --format=%s -1 && git status --short && cat src/app.rs
todoer: update second-try
 D .todoer/prs/second-try/pr.diff
 D .todoer/prs/second-try/pr.md
 D .todoer/prs/second-try/pr.patch
 D .todoer/todos/fix-the-sum.md
M  docs/guide.md
M  src/app.rs
R  src/old.rs -> src/lib.rs
fn main() {
    let a = 1;
    let b = 3;
    println!("{}", a + b);
}

$ todoer pr merge second-try
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: the patch does not apply on main - nothing changed. Ask the author to rebase the branch on main and run todoer pr submit --update:
Patch failed at 0001 Use three for b
error: Failed to merge in the changes.

$ todoer pr merge second-try --no-commit
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: the patch does not apply on main - nothing changed. Ask the author to rebase the branch on main and run todoer pr submit --update:
Applied patch to 'src/app.rs' with conflicts.

$ git log --format=%s -1 && git status --short
change app on main

$ todoer pr comment second-try 'Add a test.'
added the comment c1 on the pull request in second-try
the review is not committed - when it is done, run: git add .todoer/prs/second-try/review.md && git commit -m "Review second-try" -- .todoer/prs/second-try/review.md

$ todoer pr merge second-try
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: second-try has the unresolved comments c1 - the author must do what they ask, then run todoer pr submit --update

$ todoer pr close second-try --no-commit && git status --short
closed second-try
the todos stay: fix-the-sum - run todoer unclaim <name> to free a todo
not committed (--no-commit) - the changes are in the working tree
 D .todoer/prs/second-try/pr.diff
 D .todoer/prs/second-try/pr.md
 D .todoer/prs/second-try/pr.patch

$ todoer pr close second-try && git log --format=%s -1 && todoer pr ls
closed second-try
the todos stay: fix-the-sum - run todoer unclaim <name> to free a todo
